+    McCabe)
+
 Release 2.7.0 - 2015-04-20

   INCOMPATIBLE CHANGES

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
@Override
public FsPermission applyUMask(FsPermission umask) {
  throw new UnsupportedOperationException();
}
```
Reason:
The `applyUMask` method was incorrectly implemented in the `ImmutableFsPermission` class, throwing an `UnsupportedOperationException` when called. This misled users into thinking the method was valid, despite the class's intended immutability, leading to confusion and potential misuse.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
@Override
public void readFields(DataInput in) throws IOException {
  throw new UnsupportedOperationException();
}
```
Reason:
By removing the `applyUMask` method, the class no longer misrepresents its functionality, aligning with the intended immutability of `ImmutableFsPermission` and preventing any confusion regarding unsupported operations.

